  "reason": "The study reports a survey of researchers' opinions on publication bias in animal research, including their estimates of publication rates. However, it does not report any quantitative measure of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results, such as concordance rates or predictive values. The focus is on publication bias within animal research itself, not on the translational accuracy of animal models to human outcomes."
